Set up the fake at the protocol boundary the view model already depends on — the backend client — not inside the view model itself.

**1. Check whether a protocol boundary already exists.**

Look at how the view model gets its client today. If it takes a concrete `OrderClient` (a struct/class that does `URLSession` work), the cleanest move is to define a protocol that captures exactly the calls the view model makes, and have both the real client and your test double conform to it:

```swift
protocol OrderFetching {
    func fetchOrder(id: String) async throws -> Order
}

final class OrderClient: OrderFetching { /* real URLSession work */ }
```

Then the view model depends on `OrderFetching`, injected through its initializer:

```swift
final class OrderDetailModel {
    private let client: OrderFetching
    init(client: OrderFetching) { self.client = client }
